0.42 (Graduate student life in UC Berkeley has been a rich, rewarding experience and I) 144 664 P
-0.69 (will sorely miss it once I leave this illustrious university. I have been fortunate enough, over) 108 643 P
0.95 (the years, to meet many distinguished faculty members and intelligent colleagues, and I) 108 622 P
0.86 (have learnt much in the process. It is a pleasure to acknowledge those who have had an) 108 601 P
(impact on me, both during my time here, and in times past.) 108 580 T
1.55 (I am deeply grateful to Professor Edward A. Lee for being my advisor for this) 144 559 P
2.56 (thesis. I appreciate his patience as I kicked around looking for a thesis topic, and I) 108 538 P
-0.37 (appreciate the feedback I have received over the years, particularly about the \322big picture\323.) 108 517 P
-0.29 (I hope some of Edward\325s ability to dabble in a variety of research areas has also rubbed off) 108 496 P
(on me. I have also learned much from his insistence on good technical writing!) 108 475 T
-0.62 (I thank professors Robert K. Brayton and Donald A. Glaser for serving on my thesis) 144 454 P
1.03 (and qualifying examination committee, and professor Martin Vetterli for serving on my) 108 433 P
2.37 (qualifying examination committee. I have also greatly enjoyed attending classes here) 108 412 P
4.78 (taught by professors Richard Karp, Jean Walrand, and Donald Glaser. Professor) 108 391 P
1.09 (Messerschmitt\325s many humorous tales at the post-DSP-seminar wine-and-cheese parties) 108 370 P
(will be remembered fondly.) 108 349 T
