0.73 (This thesis is concerned with certain aspects of static scheduling of programs for) 144 500 P
1.41 (digital signal processing \050DSP\051 applications specified as dataflow graphs. In particular,) 108 479 P
0.55 (synchronous dataflow \050SDF\051, and multidimensional synchronous dataflow \050MDSDF\051 are) 108 458 P
-0.2 (two subsets of dataflow that are well suited for programming signal processing systems. A) 108 437 P
0.92 (key property that these two models have is that all scheduling decisions can be made at) 108 416 P
0.19 (compile time, rather than at run time. The thesis has two main parts: the first is a study of) 108 395 P
0.52 (the problem of minimizing the amount of code size and buffer size in the target program) 108 374 P
4.64 (when synthesizing code from a SDF or MDSDF specification. The second is a) 108 353 P
3.74 (generalization of MDSDF to permit modeling of multidimensional multirate signal) 108 332 P
(processing systems sampled on arbitrary sampling lattices.) 108 311 T
0.73 (Over the past few years, there has been increasing interest in dataflow models of) 144 290 P
4.21 (computation for DSP because of the proliferation of block diagram programming) 108 269 P
1.82 (environments for specifying and rapidly prototyping DSP systems. Dataflow is a very) 108 248 P
2.19 (natural abstraction for a block-diagram language, and many subsets of dataflow have) 108 227 P
1.95 (attractive mathematical properties that make them useful as the basis for these block-) 108 206 P
(diagram programming environments.) 108 185 T
3.12 (Visual languages have always been attractive in the engineering community,) 144 164 P
1.91 (especially in computer aided design, because engineers most often conceptualize their) 108 143 P
0.98 (systems in terms of hierarchical block diagrams or flowcharts. The 1980s witnessed the) 108 122 P
1.82 (acceptance in industry of logic-synthesis tools, in which circuits are usually described) 108 101 P
0.12 (graphically by block diagrams, and one expects the trend to continue in the evolving field) 108 80 P
