-0.35 (Hence, we need to allow infinite sequences of block executions in models designed) 144 287 P
-0.47 (to represent reactive systems. Several problems must be dealt with when infinite sequences) 108 266 P
2.65 (of actor executions are allowed. Firstly, there is the potential for buffers to become) 108 245 P
-0.24 (unbounded. Secondly, the system may deadlock, indicating that the system cannot execute) 108 224 P
-0.49 (infinitely. Even if a part of the system deadlocks, this is still an error in most practical cases) 108 203 P
-0.51 (since in a reactive system, all specified operations are assumed to operate infinitely. Lastly,) 108 182 P
0.68 (some mechanism is needed to actually sequence the actor executions in accordance with) 108 161 P
-0.69 (the precedence constraints imposed by the graph. The simplest method is to have a dynamic) 108 140 P
