-0.33 (A Petri net is a directed bipartite graph consisting of two types of nodes: places and) 144 509 P
2.67 (transitions \050see figure 1-2\051. All edges in this graph are directed between places and) 108 488 P
2.4 (transitions \050or vice-versa\051, but never between two transitions or two places. Roughly) 108 467 P
-0.57 (speaking, places correspond to edges in a dataflow graph and hold tokens. A transition fires) 108 446 P
0.08 (by removing a token from each of its input places and adding a token to each of its output) 108 425 P
0.12 (places. A place cannot have a negative number of tokens; hence, a transition can fire only) 108 404 P
0.32 (if each of its input places has at least one token. A marking is simply a function mapping) 108 383 P
(each place to a non-negative integer representing the number of tokens in that place.) 108 362 T
