0.01 (coordinates events. A variable \050representing an infinite stream of tokens\051 is aligned with a) 108 670 P
0.29 (boolean-valued clock signal, and takes on some value whenever its clock value is TRUE.) 108 649 P
-0.24 (In Esterel, a clock defines the instants in which a reaction takes place to external events. In) 108 628 P
1.25 (Signal, a powerful algebraic methodology has been devised that allows the compiler to) 108 607 P
-0.51 (reason about the signals in the system and detect inconsistencies. In SDF, there is no notion) 108 586 P
-0.74 (of a clock: synchronous simply means that the schedules constructed for SDF graphs ensure) 108 565 P
-0.01 (that data is produced and consumed at the same rate over the period of the static schedule.) 108 544 P
-0.58 (\322Synchronous\323 has also been used in the concurrency community to mean a particular style) 108 523 P
