0.38 (This is a closely related model to SDF; it has been proposed by the researchers in) 144 257 P
0.03 (the GRAPE project at K. U. Leuven [Lauw94]. In this model, an actor has several phases:) 108 236 P
0.67 (in each phase, it consumes a certain number of tokens and produces a certain number of) 108 215 P
0.08 (tokens. The numbers of tokens produced and consumed can be different for each phase of) 108 194 P
1.13 (the actor. Since the total number of phases of each actor is restricted to be finite, static) 108 173 P
-0.63 (periodic schedules can be constructed for cyclo-static graphs in a manner analogous to SDF) 108 152 P
0.13 (graphs. The main advantage of this model appears to be a lower buffering requirement on) 108 131 P
(the edges in certain types of graphs.) 108 110 T
