0.15 (The corollary provides a quick algebraic test to see if the cycle does not deadlock;) 144 488.93 P
-0.45 (if the test is negative, then we have to resort to simulation to detect deadlock. In graphs that) 108 467.93 P
3.13 (have few cycles, checking each cycle by this method might be much quicker than) 108 446.93 P
3.44 (simulation. The Karp-Miller theorem also establishes that the problem of detecting) 108 425.93 P
-0.46 (deadlock is in NP, since a non-deterministic algorithm would simply exhibit the solution to) 108 404.93 P
0.36 (the integer program if the graph deadlocks. The theorem guarantees that if the solution is) 108 383.93 P
