-0.47 (A DSP application of this more flexible data exchange is shown in figure 4-5. Here,) 144 604.91 P
1.26 (ten successive FFTs are averaged. Averaging in each frequency bin is independent and) 108 583.91 P
-0.51 (hence may proceed in parallel. The ten successive FFTs are also independent, so if all input) 108 562.91 P
2.44 (samples are available, they too may proceed in parallel. Notice here that the second) 108 541.91 P
-0.33 (dimension is being used as a temporary dimension to lay out data in a way more suitable to) 108 520.91 P
1.03 (the particular application. The analogy is that a pancake cannot be flipped over without) 108 499.91 P
0.44 (throwing it up in the air; that is, by using a third dimension. Hence, extra dimensions are) 108 478.91 P
0.94 (needed sometimes as \322workspace\323; this is exactly one of the uses in Lucid as well. The) 108 457.91 P
-0.03 (matrix multiplication specification in [Lee93] is another example where a third dimension) 108 436.91 P
-0.08 (is used to lay out data in a form more amenable to the inner product computation involved) 108 415.91 P
(in matrix multiplication.) 108 394.91 T
