0.98 (A delay in MD-SDF in associated with a tuple as shown in figure 4-8. It can be) 144 589 P
0.92 (interpreted as specifying boundary conditions on the index space. Thus, for 2D-SDF, as) 108 568 P
1.25 (shown in the figure, it specifies the number of initial rows and columns. It can also be) 108 547 P
1.26 (interpreted as specifying the direction in the index space of a dependence between two) 108 526 P
(single assignment variables, much as done in reduced dependence graphs [Kung88].) 108 505 T
1.14 (Using MD-SDF delays, the repeated inner product can be specified as shown in) 144 484 P
5.59 (figure 4-9. The only significant difference between this and figure 4-8 is the) 108 463 P
-0.5 (multidimensional delay. Its effect is illustrated schematically in figure 4-9, where the index) 108 442 P
-0.39 (space for the output of the delay is shown. The shaded area is the initial condition specified) 108 421 P
(by the delay.) 108 400 T
