0.87 (The Philips Video Signal Processor \050VSP\051 is a commercially available processor) 144 670 P
-0.42 (designed for video processing applications. A single VSP chip contains 12 arithmetic/logic) 108 649 P
-0.19 (units, 4 memory elements, 6 on-chip buffers, and ports for 6 off-chip buffers. These are all) 108 628 P
4.67 (interconnected through a full cross-point switch. Philips provides a programming) 108 607 P
-0.52 (environment for developing applications on the VSP. Programs are specified as signal flow) 108 586 P
-0.6 (graphs. Streams are one-dimensional, as in [Watl95]. Multirate operations are supported by) 108 565 P
4.7 (associating a clock period with every operation. Because all of the streams are) 108 544 P
0.5 (unidimensional, data-parallelism has to be exploited by inserting actors like multiplexors) 108 523 P
(and de-multiplexors into the signal flow graphs.) 108 502 T
