0 (A few assumptions are made about the geometry of the templates in order to make) 144 544 P
0.21 (the specification problem easier. It is observed that these assumptions are usually valid in) 108 523 P
-0.39 (practice. Access patterns are specified through two definitions: a \322fitting\323 relationship, and) 108 502 P
(a \322paving\323 relationship.) 108 481 T
0.2 (The fitting relationship specifies how elements of the multidimensional array map) 144 460 P
0.74 (into an input template \050and conversely, how elements of an output template map into an) 108 439 P
0.34 (output multidimensional array\051. This relationship is assumed to be affine, meaning that if) 108 418 P
0.16 (two \322examples\323 are given; that is, if two points and their mappings are specified, then the) 108 397 P
0.43 (mapping for filling in the rest of the template can be inferred by extrapolation. Formally,) 108 376 P
-0.15 (let) 108 355 P
-0.15 ( and) 147.94 355 P
-0.15 ( be the first two elements of the input template. Then, the user specifies,) 196.05 355 P
-0.14 (using the GUI, the two points) 108 334 P
