-0.14 ( and) 519.81 334 P
0.31 (. By extrapolating the line from) 133.09 313 P
0.31 ( to) 297.57 313 P
0.31 ( in the multidimensional array, the remaining) 321.18 313 P
(elements of the template can be filled in.) 108 292 T
2.03 (The paving relationship specifies how translations of the template in the input) 144 271 P
3.79 (multidimensional array affect the translations of the output template in the output) 108 250 P
-0.69 (multidimensional array. This relationship is also assumed to be affine so that two examples,) 108 229 P
0.23 (specified graphically in the GUI, are sufficient to specify the entire tiling of the input and) 108 208 P
0.64 (output multidimensional arrays. The execution of the graph then proceeds by firing each) 108 187 P
-0.44 (computational node as many times as needed to completely fill its output multidimensional) 108 166 P
(arrays.) 108 145 T
