-0.04 (It is hoped that the AOL formalism will eliminate or at least ameliorate this problem. This) 108 586 P
-0.53 (should result in faster design times, visual programs that are understood more easily, which) 108 565 P
(can then be maintained or modified or debugged much more easily.) 108 544 T
-0.28 (The development of AOL has been in response to actual needs of signal processing) 144 523 P
3.08 (systems designers at Thomson, and thus, should be of help to such designers. The) 108 502 P
1.4 (formalism also opens up several research issues such as designing efficient schedulers,) 108 481 P
-0.21 (exploiting data parallelism effectively, implications for code generation for programmable) 108 460 P
3.7 (video signal processing architectures, \050none of which have been dealt with yet in) 108 439 P
-0.72 ([Deme94]\051, and better visualization techniques for these access patterns. Currently, in order) 108 418 P
