-0.2 (has to be visualized using 2 dimensional projections. Since arrays with dimensions of upto) 108 376 P
1.03 (7 are not uncommon, the number of 2 dimensional projections can become too large; it) 108 355 P
-0.02 (would be cumbersome to have to deal with each of these sequentially for the designer \050for) 108 334 P
-0.07 (example, a 7 dimensional array has 21 2-dimensional projections\051. Although it is not clear) 108 313 P
