0.49 (We have described an extension of MDSDF to handle arbitrary sampling lattices.) 144 223 P
0.79 (The key extensions have been to associate two parameters for each arc in the graph: the) 108 202 P
-0.27 (sampling lattice for the data on that arc, and a \322support matrix\323 that describes the region of) 108 181 P
-0.43 (the space where current data has been produced. Equivalently, these two parameters can be) 108 160 P
2.7 (specified for source actors, and can be determined for the other arcs by tracing the) 108 139 P
0.52 (operations that each node in the graph performs. Since decimation and expansion are the) 108 118 P
4.64 (only two actors \050of signal processing interest\051 that change lattices, it should be) 108 97 P
-0.23 (straightforward to determine the lattice and support matrix for every arc in the graph given) 108 76 P
