(Conclusion and Future Work) 210.74 564 T
0 12 Q
0.01 (In this thesis, we have solved several scheduling problems for programs expressed) 144 500 P
0.07 (as SDF and MDSDF graphs. Since the potentially large rate changes in SDF and MDSDF) 108 479 P
0.16 (specifications can result in a code and buffer-memory size explosion, a primary focus has) 108 458 P
2.92 (been on generating schedules that minimize code and data memory size. Code size) 108 437 P
4.38 (optimality is obtained by generating single appearance schedules. Algorithms and) 108 416 P
2.01 (heuristics are given that generate single appearance schedules optimized for buffering) 108 395 P
1.8 (memory. In particular, three basic algorithms are developed and discussed: a dynamic) 108 374 P
0.18 (programming algorithm that is used for post-optimization, and two heuristics: RPMC and) 108 353 P
-0.16 (APGAN. These two algorithms are complementary in the way they approach the problem,) 108 332 P
1 (and an extensive experimental study confirms this by showing that for graphs that have) 108 311 P
-0.39 (irregular topologies and rate changes, RPMC exhibits better performance, while for graphs) 108 290 P
-0.02 (having regular topologies and rate changes, APGAN performs better. In addition APGAN) 108 269 P
1.74 (is optimal for a class of SDF graphs that includes several practical systems. All these) 108 248 P
0.52 (algorithms are shown to extend to MDSDF also. The three algorithms discussed have all) 108 227 P
(been implemented in the Ptolemy framework, in the SDF domain.) 108 206 T
0.48 (In Chapter 5, the thesis shifts focus to a rather different type of problem: namely,) 144 185 P
1.26 (generalizing the MDSDF model to permit arbitrary sampling lattices. Multidimensional) 108 164 P
0.48 (multirate systems sampled on non-rectangular lattices are interesting and useful, and it is) 108 143 P
-0.09 (desirable to have a dataflow model capable of expressing such systems. We generalize the) 108 122 P
1.59 (MDSDF model, and show that the key property of compile-time schedulability can be) 108 101 P
-0.3 (retained in the generalized model. In particular, we show that in the generalized model, the) 108 80 P
